From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:37:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add getrandom's custom backend for AROS
 (wordcraft-aros-entropy)

Problem: wordcraft-docx draws the salts and keys of encrypted saves from
  getrandom 0.3, which has no AROS backend; the x86_64 ABIv11 link of
  wordcraft-cli failed with __getrandom_v03_custom undefined.
Rationale: the build selects --cfg getrandom_backend="custom"; this crate
  defines the backend over the AROS C library's getentropy(), which fails
  rather than returning weak bytes. It is the PhotoCraft AROS port's
  photocraft-aros-entropy, renamed. wordcraft-docx links it on AROS, so
  every program that can write an encrypted document has it.
Scope: AROS only; other targets do not build the crate's code.
Upstream-status: local-only.
Verification: wordcraft-cli links for x86_64 ABIv11 with no undefined
  symbols; not run in this commit.
Removal: when getrandom has an AROS backend.
